<Base title="Start here" lang="en" description="Choose who you are and get the parts of the law that matter to you.">
  <h1>Start here. Who are you?</h1>
  <p>The law treats a grocer and a bank differently, and treats you as a customer differently from you as an employer. Pick the description that fits, and we will show only what applies.</p>
  <div class="tiles">
    <a class="tile" href="/en/pathways/citizen-pathway/"><strong>An ordinary person</strong><span>Student · employee · parent · online shopper. About 20 minutes.</span></a>
    <a class="tile" href="/en/pathways/small-business-guide/"><strong>A small business owner</strong><span>Grocery · retail · restaurant · salon · tuition · clinic · online seller · freelancer. The guide, then the <a href="/en/pathways/small-business-checklist/">checklist</a>.</span></a>
    <a class="tile" href="/en/pathways/organisation-pathway/"><strong>Someone in a larger organisation</strong><span>Company · bank · hospital · school · IT and BPO · telecom · government.</span></a>
    <a class="tile" href="/en/pathways/technical-pathway/"><strong>An IT, security, compliance or legal professional</strong><span>Sysadmin · developer · security · DPO · compliance · lawyer.</span></a>
  </div>
  <h2>Not sure?</h2>
  <p>Most people are two of these at once — an employee during the day and a customer in the evening. Start with "ordinary person"; it is the shortest.</p>
</Base>
